  "reply_text": "Found **one merge-blocking issue** in `sms-segments` against `main`:\n\n**[P1] `fits_one_segment()` counts characters, not UTF-8 bytes** — `sms/segment.py:5`\n`len(text)` violates the documented 160-byte limit and incorrectly marks multibyte messages as a single segment. Reproduced with:\n- `'é' * 81`: 162 bytes → returns `True`, but `segment_count()` returns **2**.\n- `'😀' * 41`: 164 bytes → same mismatch.\n\nThis can classify a message as one text even though the cost calculation bills it as two. Use the existing `utf8_len()` helper for the comparison, and add tests at and just above the 160-byte boundary for accented characters and emoji.\n\nAll **4 existing tests pass**, but the segment-fit tests cover only ASCII. No other issues found under the repo’s documented UTF-8/160-byte model. No files changed.",
